WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.630
Times tables get easier with tricks. Let's learn one for fives and one for nines.

00:07.080 --> 00:12.821
Multiples of five always end in zero or five. Five, ten, fifteen, twenty,

00:12.821 --> 00:14.394
twenty-five, thirty.

00:14.844 --> 00:22.995
For five times six, think of half of ten times six. Ten times six is sixty. Half of sixty is thirty.

00:23.445 --> 00:30.699
For nines, multiply by ten and then take away the number. Nine times six is ten times six,

00:30.699 --> 00:34.729
which is sixty, take away six. That is fifty-four.

00:35.179 --> 00:42.791
Here is a check. The digits of every nine fact add up to nine. Fifty-four has a five and a four,

00:42.791 --> 00:44.932
and five plus four is nine.
